    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_457e3defad9fb544e4cc496c5aa9c970de83ad1e8875817e83cd0c39e5295d4f",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source-grounded: under RH the zero sum F(s) is nonnegative; shifting right, integrating the logarithmic derivative, and inserting a smoothed explicit formula let one choose the shift so F's coefficient is nonpositive and may be dropped. Conceptual reading: the proof controls zeros by engineering their sign rather than estimating them individually.",
