    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d659bb2b4fc765f2c4ae1f78e5c87eeb4debe93a7ec175459f5d89f04b3cb6a3",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The pointwise argument first uses RH to make the zero sum nonnegative and chooses the horizontal shift so its residual coefficient is nonpositive, leaving a smoothed von Mangoldt upper bound; the next unit then decomposes the nonprime terms, bounding powers of exponent at least three by O(1) and prime squares by O(log log log T), so the usable bound is reduced to primes at that error scale.",
