    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_fc850fc8f3cebfee34a658fab543cd18ca40c2ceb65590b92057aac1736ba496",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The high-moment lemma converts a short prime Dirichlet polynomial into factorially weighted diagonal data under the capacity constraint x^k <= T/log T. The theorem then chooses the cutoff and splits the polynomial into small- and large-prime pieces, forces one piece to be large, and assigns each piece an admissible moment order suited to its variance and length, producing the quadratic moderate-tail and V log V extreme-tail bounds.",
